  data: {
    LLM: "Prioritize making a scoring move over simply getting rid of high tiles. A 4-point move (sum 12) is worth more than 'dumping' a Double-6 for no points.\n\nBlocking: If you cannot score, play a tile that makes the end total a number that is difficult for the opponent to divide by 3 (like 7, 8, or 11).\n\nBoneyard Management: If you have a strong hand, try to 'clog' the ends with values you don't have, forcing the opponent to draw from the boneyard and increase their hand size (and your eventual domino bonus).",
    Player: "Prioritize making a scoring move over simply getting rid of high tiles. A 4-point move (sum 12) is worth more than 'dumping' a Double-6 for no points.\n\nBlocking: If you cannot score, play a tile that makes the end total a number that is difficult for the opponent to divide by 3 (like 7, 8, or 11).\n\nBoneyard Management: If you have a strong hand, try to 'clog' the ends with values you don't have, forcing the opponent to draw from the boneyard and increase their hand size (and your eventual domino bonus).",
